          <h3>Website enquiry to booked appointment</h3>
          <dl>
            <div><dt>Challenge</dt><dd>Enquiries arrive through the website, WhatsApp, Google and the phone. Receptionists retype each one into the schedule and reply by hand.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Automation solution</dt><dd>One intake workflow collects every channel, an AI step reads the request, and patients choose an open slot themselves.</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <details class="case">
            <summary>View case study <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></summary>
            <ol>
              <li><span><b>Capture.</b> The website form, WhatsApp Business and Google Business messages all feed one n8n webhook.</span></li>
              <li><span><b>Understand.</b> An AI step pulls out the treatment, preferred times and urgency, and flags pain or swelling for staff.</span></li>
              <li><span><b>Offer.</b> The calendar returns open slots, and the patient picks one from a short message.</span></li>
              <li><span><b>Confirm.</b> The booking is written to the practice software and a reminder is scheduled for the day before.</span></li>
            </ol>
          </details>
        </div>
        <div class="preview" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="mini-flow">
            <div class="node"><b>3 channels</b><span class="mono">web · wa · google</span></div><span class="arrow">&rarr;</span>
