          </div>
        </div>
        <h3>Recalls and reviews on autopilot</h3>
        <dl>
          <div><dt>Challenge</dt><dd>The recall list grows every month, and nobody has time to contact overdue patients or ask happy ones for a review.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Automation solution</dt><dd>Each week the workflow finds patients who are due, sends a personal message with a booking link, and asks for a review after the visit.</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <details class="case">
          <summary>View case study <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></summary>
          <ol>
            <li><span><b>Find.</b> The workflow pulls patients due for a check-up or cleaning from the practice software.</span></li>
            <li><span><b>Write.</b> AI personalizes each message with the patient's name and last treatment.</span></li>
            <li><span><b>Book.</b> The message includes a link to open slots, so patients book without calling.</span></li>
            <li><span><b>Review.</b> After the visit, a short review request goes out. Staff see any negative feedback first.</span></li>
          </ol>
        </details>
      </article>
